## 3. Centralized Theme System

The theme is managed **entirely via CSS custom properties (design tokens)**. Every component, every Shadcn/ui primitive, and Tailwind utilities all resolve to these tokens — so changing one token set instantly re-themes the whole app.

### 3.1 Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["tokens.css<br/>(CSS Custom Properties)"] --> B["Tailwind Config<br/>maps utilities → tokens"]
    A --> C["Shadcn/ui Components<br/>consume tokens directly"]
    A --> D["Custom Components<br/>use var(--token-name)"]
    E["ThemeProvider"] -->|"sets data-theme attr<br/>on document root"| A
    F["Zustand Theme Store"] -->|"selected theme + overrides"| E
    G["Theme Switcher UI"] --> F
```

### 3.2 Design Token Categories

All visual decisions are expressed as tokens in `styles/tokens.css`:

| Category | Token Examples | What They Control |
|---|---|---|
| **Colors** | `--color-primary`, `--color-primary-foreground`, `--color-destructive` | Brand colors, semantic colors |
| **Surfaces** | `--color-background`, `--color-card`, `--color-popover`, `--color-muted` | Backgrounds, cards, panels |
| **Borders** | `--color-border`, `--color-ring`, `--radius-sm/md/lg` | Borders, focus rings, rounding |
| **Typography** | `--font-sans`, `--font-mono`, `--font-size-*`, `--font-weight-*` | Font families, sizes, weights |
| **Spacing** | `--spacing-*` | Consistent spacing scale |
| **Shadows** | `--shadow-sm/md/lg` | Elevation levels |
| **Charts** | `--chart-1` through `--chart-5` | Dashboard chart palette |

### 3.3 Theme Presets

Each preset is a CSS file that overrides the tokens on `[data-theme="<name>"]`:

```css
/* styles/tokens.css — defaults (light) */
:root {
  --color-primary: 220 90% 56%;
  --color-background: 0 0% 100%;
  --color-card: 0 0% 100%;
  --radius-md: 0.5rem;
  --font-sans: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  /* ... full token set */
}

/* styles/themes/dark.css */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --color-primary: 220 90% 64%;
  --color-background: 224 10% 10%;
  --color-card: 224 10% 13%;
  /* only override what changes */
}
```

### 3.4 ThemeProvider & Store

```ts
// core/theme/theme-store.ts
interface ThemeState {
  activeTheme: 'light' | 'dark' | 'system' | string; // string = custom gym theme
  overrides: Partial<ThemeTokens>;                    // runtime token overrides
  setTheme: (theme: string) => void;
  setTokenOverride: (token: string, value: string) => void;
  resetOverrides: () => void;
}
```

```tsx
// core/theme/theme-provider.tsx
// Wraps the app in <App /> via providers.tsx
// - Reads activeTheme from store
// - Sets `data-theme` attribute on <html>
// - Applies any runtime overrides as inline CSS vars on :root
// - Listens to system `prefers-color-scheme` when set to 'system'
```

### 3.5 How Components Consume Tokens

Every component uses tokens — **never hard-coded colors**:

```tsx
// Tailwind utilities map to tokens via tailwind.config.ts
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border rounded-md shadow-md">

// Direct CSS when needed
<div style={{ color: 'hsl(var(--color-primary))' }}>

// Shadcn/ui components already use tokens internally — no changes needed
<Button variant="default">Save</Button>  // uses --color-primary automatically
```

### 3.6 Theme Switcher Component

A dropdown in the app header lets users switch themes at runtime:

```
┌──────────────────────────┐
│  🎨 Theme               │
│  ○ Light                 │
│  ● Dark                  │
│  ○ System                │
│  ──────────────────────  │
│  ○ Gym Brand (custom)    │
└──────────────────────────┘
```

The selection is persisted to `localStorage` and restored on load.

### 3.7 Gym-Branded Themes (Future)

Gym owners will be able to set brand colors in **Settings → Appearance**, which creates runtime token overrides stored in the database. This allows each gym to white-label the UI with zero code changes.

---

## 4. Multi-Tenancy Strategy (Frontend)

The BRD mandates strict data isolation per gym. The frontend enforces this:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Axios Interceptor               │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │ Every request automatically injects:    │ │
│  │  • Authorization: Bearer <jwt>          │ │
│  │  • X-Tenant-Id: <gymId from auth store> │ │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- **JWT token** contains `tenantId`, `role`, and `branchId`
- **Zustand auth store** exposes `currentTenant` and `currentBranch`
- **Axios interceptor** attaches `X-Tenant-Id` header to every API call
- **Super Admin** can switch tenants via a gym selector in the header
- **TanStack Query keys** include `tenantId` to prevent cache cross-contamination

---

## 5. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

### 4.1 Route-Level Guards

```tsx
// Usage in router.tsx
<Route element={<RoleGuard allowed={["Owner", "Receptionist"]} />}>
  <Route path="members" element={<MembersListPage />} />
</Route>
```

### 4.2 Permission Matrix

| Feature | Super Admin | Owner | Receptionist | Trainer | Member |
|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| Dashboard (full) | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Manage Gyms | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Member CRUD | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| View Own Profile | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Membership Packages | ✅ | ✅ | View | ❌ | View |
| Payments | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | View Own |
| Trainer Management | ✅ | ✅ | View | ❌ | ❌ |
| Trainer Schedule | ✅ | ✅ | View | Own | ❌ |
| Attendance Check-in | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Self |
| Reports & Export | ✅ | ✅ | Limited | ❌ | ❌ |

### 4.3 Sidebar Navigation

The sidebar renders **different menu items per role**, driven by a config:
```ts
const NAV_CONFIG = [
  { label: "Dashboard", path: "/dashboard", icon: LayoutDashboard, roles: ["SuperAdmin", "Owner"] },
  { label: "Members",   path: "/members",   icon: Users,           roles: ["SuperAdmin", "Owner", "Receptionist"] },
  // ...
];
```

---

## 6. Routing Architecture

```
/                           → Redirect based on role
/register                   → Gym registration (public)
/login                      → Login page (public)
/setup-wizard               → Post-registration setup (Owner only)
  /setup-wizard/profile
  /setup-wizard/plans
  /setup-wizard/staff
  /setup-wizard/payments

/dashboard                  → Owner Dashboard
/members                    → Member list
/members/new                → Add member
/members/:id                → Member detail / profile
/members/:id/renew          → Membership renewal

/memberships                → Package list
/memberships/new            → Create package
/memberships/:id/edit       → Edit package

/trainers                   → Trainer list
/trainers/new               → Add trainer
/trainers/:id               → Trainer profile & schedule
/trainers/:id/schedule      → Schedule management

/payments                   → Payment list / financial dashboard
/payments/:id/invoice       → Invoice view

/attendance                 → Attendance log
/attendance/check-in        → Check-in page

/reports                    → Reports hub
/reports/:type              → Specific report (revenue, membership, trainer, etc.)

/settings                   → Gym settings, branches, staff
/admin/gyms                 → Super Admin gym management
```

All routes under `/` (except `/register`, `/login`) are wrapped in `<AuthGuard>` and `<AppLayout>`.

---

## 7. State Management Strategy

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Zustand Store"] -->|"Auth, UI theme, sidebar state"| B["Client-only state"]
    C["TanStack Query"] -->|"Members, packages, payments..."| D["Server state cache"]
    E["React Hook Form"] -->|"Form fields, validation"| F["Form state"]
    D -->|"Optimistic updates"| C
    C -->|"Auto refetch, pagination"| D
```

| State Type | Tool | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Auth / Session** | Zustand | Current user, tenant, role, token |
| **Theme** | Zustand + CSS Vars | Active theme preset, runtime token overrides |
| **UI State** | Zustand | Sidebar collapsed, active branch |
| **Server Data** | TanStack Query | Members list, packages, dashboard stats |
| **Form Data** | React Hook Form | Registration form, payment form |

---

## 8. API Layer Design

Each feature module has an `api/` folder with **custom hooks** that wrap TanStack Query:

```ts
// features/members/api/use-members.ts
export function useMembers(filters: MemberFilters) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ["members", tenantId, filters],
    queryFn: () => api.get("/members", { params: filters }),
  });
}

export function useCreateMember() {
  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: (data: CreateMemberDto) => api.post("/members", data),
    onSuccess: () => queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["members"] }),
  });
}
```

---

## 9. Key UI Patterns

### 8.1 Dashboard Widgets
Reusable `<StatCard>` component with icon, label, value, and trend indicator. Dashboard page composes 6 widgets matching BRD §6.1.

### 8.2 Data Tables
All list pages (members, trainers, payments, packages) use a shared `<DataTable>` component built on TanStack Table with:
- Server-side pagination
- Column sorting
- Global & column filters
- Row actions menu
- Bulk selection (future)

### 8.3 Setup Wizard
Multi-step wizard using a stepper component with 4 stages (Profile → Plans → Staff → Payment Settings). Progress is persisted to the backend after each step.

### 8.4 Report Export
`<ExportButton>` component that accepts table data and exports to:
- **PDF** via jsPDF + autoTable
- **Excel** via SheetJS

### 8.5 Notifications System
In-app notification bell with a dropdown, powered by polling or WebSocket (future). Toast notifications for real-time feedback on actions.

---

## 10. Performance Strategy

| Technique | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Code Splitting** | `React.lazy()` + `Suspense` per feature route |
| **Query Caching** | TanStack Query with stale times tuned per entity |
| **Virtualization** | `@tanstack/react-virtual` for large member/payment lists |
| **Image Optimization** | Lazy load profile photos, compress on upload |
| **Bundle Analysis** | `rollup-plugin-visualizer` in Vite config |

---

## 11. Future-Proofing

| Future BRD Item | Architecture Support |
|---|---|
| Mobile App | API hooks in `features/*/api/` are framework-agnostic — reusable in React Native |
| Payment Gateway | `payments/` feature already modular; add gateway adapter in `core/api/` |
| SMS Reminders | Backend concern; frontend adds notification preferences UI in settings |
| Workout Tracking | Add new `features/workouts/` module — zero impact on existing modules |
| SaaS Billing | Add `features/billing/` module for subscription management |

---

## 12. Verification Plan

Since this is an architecture proposal (no code yet), verification will happen during implementation:

### Automated Tests
- **Unit Tests**: Vitest for utility functions, custom hooks, and Zod schemas
- **Component Tests**: React Testing Library for form components and data tables
- **E2E Tests**: Playwright for critical flows (login → dashboard, member CRUD, payment recording)
- Run with: `npm run test` (Vitest) and `npx playwright test` (E2E)

### Manual Verification
- After scaffolding, verify the dev server starts: `npm run dev`
- Verify route navigation and lazy loading in browser DevTools Network tab
- Verify role-based sidebar rendering by mocking different user roles

